      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Introducing the Gemini Decisions API, powered by our new Gemini Decision 1 model.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/developers-tools/gemini-decisions-api/",
        "source": "Google (The Keyword · AI)",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-11T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-12T02:54:36.966Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "We are introducing the Gemini Decisions API to help you make fast, probabilistic choices across text, images, audio, video, and PDFs.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/developers-tools/gemini-decisions-api/",
        "source": "Google (The Keyword · AI)",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-11T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-12T02:54:36.966Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Today, we’re introducing the Gemini Decisions API, a new endpoint for fast, closed-set decisions powered by our new Gemini Decision 1 model (gemini-decision-1), available through the Gemini API in Google AI Studio .",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/developers-tools/gemini-decisions-api/",
        "source": "Google (The Keyword · AI)",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-11T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-12T02:54:36.966Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "On benchmarks spanning agent routing, reasoning, ranking, and multimodal understanding, Gemini Decision 1 leads across the suite, with the lowest calibration error.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/developers-tools/gemini-decisions-api/",
        "source": "Google (The Keyword · AI)",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-11T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-12T02:54:36.966Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Gemini Decision 1 scores options without token-by-token decoding, keeping median latency 50-100 ms of model compute (150-250 ms end-to-end), across multimodal inputs and contexts up to 16K tokens, remaining nearly flat from 1 to 100 questions per request.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/developers-tools/gemini-decisions-api/",
        "source": "Google (The Keyword · AI)",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-11T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-12T02:54:36.966Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E11",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "With zero output tokens billed, Gemini Decision 1 with the Decisions API is nearly 5x cheaper across the shared benchmark suite than Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite with the Interactions API.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/developers-tools/gemini-decisions-api/",
        "source": "Google (The Keyword · AI)",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-11T00:00:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-12T02:54:36.966Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E12",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Built on Gemini’s native multimodal architecture, Gemini Decision 1 can process text, images, audio, video, and PDFs directly in a single forward pass.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://blog.google/innovation-and-ai/technology/developers-tools/gemini-decisions-api/",
        "source": "Google (The Keyword · AI)",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-11T00:00:00.000Z",
